license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  A mechanism case study on whether LLMs generalize a bug fix to a represented
  predicate or merely tabulate the reported case. On a verifier soundness bug
  whose correct fix is an XOR-shaped predicate, it isolates where prompt-encoded
  methods, an execution-gated evaluation tool, and cross-model capability each
  do or do not lift the fix, and shows that enumeration is inducible by the model
  while calibration (external ground truth) is not. Includes the forced-fresh
  grading harness, the case arms (codex and Fable), the full reasoning trail, and
  reproduction instructions.
